@page
@model CommunityHub.Pages.Organizer.SponsorAdmin.DashboardModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Sponsor maintenance";
}

<div class="card">
    <h1>Sponsor maintenance</h1>
    @if (Model.AccessDenied)
    {
        <p class="error">This area is for organizers only.</p>
        <p><a asp-page="/Index">Back to hub</a></p>
    }
    else
    {
        @* 🔴 §1085 — the per-company STATUS TABLE is gone; status lives in one place for every role
           now. The link is not a courtesy: the operator asked for the second board to be retired
           precisely because two of them disagreed, and a retired page with no forwarding address is
           how somebody ends up trusting a bookmark to a board that no longer exists. *@
        <p>The sponsor maintenance actions — contact sync, coordinator migration, Zoho provisioning
           and the ERP&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;webshop reconcile.</p>
        <p style="font-size:13.5px;color:#555;">
            Looking for sponsor <strong>status</strong>? It moved to
            <a asp-page="/Organizer/ParticipantStatus" asp-route-role="@ParticipantRole.Sponsor">Participant status</a>,
            one board for every role — completion per company, what is still open, and overdue tasks.
            Stage-by-stage detail stays on
            <a asp-page="/Organizer/SponsorDeliverables">Sponsor deliverables</a>.
        </p>
        <p><a asp-page="/Organizer/SponsorAdmin/Index">&larr; Back to Sponsor Admin</a></p>

        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Model.ActionMessage))
        {
            <p class="info" role="status">@Model.ActionMessage</p>
        }

        <div style="margin:10px 0 16px;padding:12px 14px;background:#eff6ff;border:1px solid #bfdbfe;border-left:4px solid #2563eb;border-radius:8px;">
            <strong>Webshop → Zoho maintenance.</strong>
            <p style="margin:4px 0 8px;font-size:13.5px;color:#374151;">
                Fill each sponsor's Event Coordinator from the webshop default coordinator (only where empty — CEH owns it once set),
                then re-sync every sponsor record to Zoho Backstage. This also corrects the older UTF-8 mojibake (æ/ø/å) in Zoho.
            </p>
            <form method="post" asp-page-handler="MigrateResync" style="display:inline;margin:0;">
                <button type="submit" data-ceh-confirm="confirmMigrateResync" data-ceh-count="@Model.CompanyCount">Migrate coordinators &amp; re-sync all to Event System (Zoho)</button>
            </form>
            <form method="post" asp-page-handler="Provision" style="display:inline;margin:0 0 0 8px;">
                <button type="submit" data-ceh-confirm="confirmProvision" data-ceh-count="@Model.CompanyCount">Create / link missing in Event System (Zoho)</button>
            </form>
            <form method="post" asp-page-handler="ReconcileErp" style="display:inline;margin:0 0 0 8px;">
                <button type="submit" data-ceh-confirm="confirmReconcileErp">Reconcile ERP → webshop (users + defaults)</button>
            </form>
            @* §496c — the missing LAST leg. The buttons above push ERP → webshop; this PULLS
               webshop → hub, so a contact added directly in Company Manager shows up in CEH without
               waiting for the scheduled pull. Idempotent — pressing it twice changes nothing. *@
            <form method="post" asp-page-handler="SyncContacts" style="display:inline;margin:0 0 0 8px;">
                <button type="submit">Sync contacts webshop → hub (now)</button>
            </form>
            @* §1158 — the one-time public-name sweep. PREVIEW is a separate, unconfirmed button on
               purpose: it writes nothing, so making him confirm it would train him to click through
               the confirmation that actually matters. *@
            <form method="post" asp-page-handler="NormalizePublicNames" style="display:inline;margin:0 0 0 8px;">
                <input type="hidden" name="apply" value="false" />
                <button type="submit">Preview public-name cleanup (A/S, ApS, GmbH &hellip;)</button>
            </form>

            @* §1173 — when a sponsor re-registers under a new VAT number it becomes a NEW company:
               new contract, new ERP customer, new webshop company. The contract belongs to the legal
               entity, but the logo and description belong to the organisation — so they are carried
               forward rather than asked for a second time. *@
            <div style="margin-top:12px;padding:10px 12px;background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:8px;">
                <strong style="font-size:13.5px;">Company re-registered under a new legal entity?</strong>
                <p style="margin:4px 0 8px;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b7280;">
                    Carries logo, descriptions, website, LinkedIn and coordinator from the old company
                    to the new one. Never copies Zoho ids, ERP links or anything the orders decide, and
                    only fills fields that are still empty. The new company needs its first completed
                    order before it has a record to copy into.
                </p>
                <form method="post" asp-page-handler="CarryForward" style="display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin:0;">
                    <input type="text" name="fromCompanyId" placeholder="From company id" required style="width:140px;" />
                    <input type="text" name="toCompanyId" placeholder="To company id" required style="width:140px;" />
                    <button type="submit" name="apply" value="false">Preview</button>
                    <button type="submit" name="apply" value="true" data-ceh-confirm="confirmCarryForward">Carry it forward</button>
                </form>
            </div>
            <form method="post" asp-page-handler="NormalizePublicNames" style="display:inline;margin:0 0 0 8px;">
                <input type="hidden" name="apply" value="true" />
                <button type="submit" data-ceh-confirm="confirmNormalizeNames">Apply public-name cleanup</button>
            </form>
            <p style="font-size:12px;color:#6b7280;margin:8px 0 0;">
                <strong>Create / link</strong> provisions sponsors/exhibitors that don't exist in Zoho yet (replaces the legacy sync script — also runs automatically after each order pull when enabled).
            </p>
        </div>
        <partial name="_ConfirmModal" model='new CommunityHub.Pages.Shared.ConfirmModalModel(
            Id: "confirmProvision",
            Title: "Create / link sponsors in Zoho?",
            Body: "This creates or links {count} sponsor compan(ies) in Zoho Backstage from webshop data. Existing/linked companies are left unchanged. Continue?",
            ConfirmLabel: "Run it",
            CancelLabel: "Cancel",
            DefaultCount: Model.CompanyCount.ToString())' />
        <partial name="_ConfirmModal" model='new CommunityHub.Pages.Shared.ConfirmModalModel(
            Id: "confirmReconcileErp",
            Title: "Reconcile ERP to webshop?",
            Body: "This creates missing Company Manager users from the backend group-1 contacts and sets each company default signer + event coordinator from the contact roles (never overwriting a curated default). Contacts missing a Role:1/Role:2 are emailed to the organizer. Continue?",
            ConfirmLabel: "Run it",
            CancelLabel: "Cancel")' />
        <partial name="_ConfirmModal" model='new CommunityHub.Pages.Shared.ConfirmModalModel(
            Id: "confirmCarryForward",
            Title: "Carry the sponsor profile forward?",
            Body: "This copies logo, descriptions, website, LinkedIn and coordinator from the old company to the new one, filling only fields that are still empty. The old company is left untouched, and nothing that the orders decide is copied. Continue?",
            ConfirmLabel: "Carry it forward",
            CancelLabel: "Cancel")' />
        <partial name="_ConfirmModal" model='new CommunityHub.Pages.Shared.ConfirmModalModel(
            Id: "confirmNormalizeNames",
            Title: "Remove legal forms from public names?",
            Body: "This rewrites the PUBLIC company name in the webshop for every sponsor whose name ends in a legal form (A/S, ApS, GmbH, LLC, K/S, AG …), so the audience-facing name reads like a brand. The billing/legal name is NOT touched. Sponsors can edit their public name afterwards and this will not run again on its own. Preview it first if you have not. Continue?",
            ConfirmLabel: "Rewrite the names",
            CancelLabel: "Cancel")' />
        <partial name="_ConfirmModal" model='new CommunityHub.Pages.Shared.ConfirmModalModel(
            Id: "confirmMigrateResync",
            Title: "Migrate coordinators & re-sync to Zoho?",
            Body: "This fills missing Event Coordinators from the webshop and re-syncs {count} sponsor compan(ies) to Zoho Backstage, overwriting the synced fields there. Continue?",
            ConfirmLabel: "Run it",
            CancelLabel: "Cancel",
            DefaultCount: Model.CompanyCount.ToString())' />

        @* 🗑 §784.3/§784.6 — the "Zoho pipeline not yet configured" notice is GONE.
           Operator 2026-08-03: it *"seems wrong"* — and it was. It described Zoho OAuth as unwired
           and pointed at a setup checklist, while Zoho has been syncing sponsors for months; its
           only real subject was the LEAD counters, which are removed below because the feature is
           switched off. A warning that describes a state the system left long ago is worse than no
           warning: it teaches the reader that the banners on this page are not to be believed. *@
    }
</div>

@* 🗑 §1085 — THE PER-COMPANY STATUS TABLE WAS HERE (company · contacts · tasks done/total ·
   overdue · last Zoho sync), plus the "+N former sponsors hidden" line that explained its
   omissions. Both are retired: status is now ONE board for every role at /Organizer/ParticipantStatus,
   which reads each participant's WIZARD rather than counting tasks a second way. Counting them a
   second way is exactly what let this page and the deliverables board disagree — the reason the
   operator said he trusted neither. The four maintenance actions above are what this page is now. *@
